into a higher level of resources...but that level is finite also.(e.g.
developing the capability to mine the asteroids....plenty of metals,
little organics)
Bottom line is that the whole system can be considered a dynamic quantum
system...there are limiting levels, but these limits are flexible...
(Sorry if this seems a little Zen-like....)

The economical ecological solution is to use the knowledge gained from the
lower cycles and apply it to the higher ones...(An example...Man has
learned that he cannot shit directly on a garden and hope to recycle the
organics he eats...it must be composted (read "processed") first...Applied
to a higher cycle...you CANNOT dump "unprocessed" radioactive waste on the
environment and expect to get away with it. Convet it to a form that can
be used...by "composting".)

I firmly feel that we can solve our current environmental crises by
properly applying the knowledge gained from lower cycles to the larger
ones. 
What did we learn from the Bio-sphere....? 

