Date: Fri, 28 Jan 94 16:16:46 EST
Subject: [#94-1-652] META: go decentrally moderate yourself

It seems to me that a centralized scheme is inappropriate, given the
ideology underlying this list.  How about adding these commands:

::moderator foo
	When bar sends this command, bar is saying that he only wants
	to see messages that foo has approved. 
::approve #94-1-643
	When foo sends this command, this message is marked as
	approved by foo, and it will be sent to all people who have selected
	foo as the moderator.

We could have the same suite of commands related to approval that are
related to including: ::approve all, ::disapprove all, etc.

The additional space required would be the same as the space presently
required to keep track of which messages each person has seen for the
::filterlist command.

We might also add
::permit-moderate bar
	foo sends this command to permit bar to give the command
	::moderator bar.  This allows foo to charge fees for moderation.
::forbid-moderate bar
	foo sends this command when bar's subscription to foo's
	services has expired.

Perhaps aspiring moderators should pay a higher subscription fee to
support all the machinery.

By the way, has EXI tried to become host for some other mailing lists?
It seems a shame to limit the use of the list software to the small
number of people interested in being in the extropians list.

